<title>FINLAND: Finnish raw wood prices rise further in Aug -METLA.</title>
<headline>Finnish raw wood prices rise further in Aug -METLA.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish raw wood stumpage prices continued to rise in August (weeks 32-35) after soaring in July (weeks 28-31) amid difficulties to reach regional price agreements, the Finnish Forest Research Institute METLA said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Pulpwood stumpage prices (markka per cubic metre):</p>
<p>	     Aug '96    Jul '96     1995	H2 '95	H1 '95</p>
<p> Pine	  86.90	85.20    93.00	 93.20	 92.90</p>
<p> Spruce     115.00     110.60   109.70	109.00	110.20</p>
<p> Birch	 87.70	84.60    98.20	 98.00	 98.40</p>
<p>Logwood stumpage prices (markka per cubic metre):</p>
<p>	     Aug '96    Jul '96     1995	 H2 '95     H1 '95</p>
<p> Pine	 239.30     239.30   247.10	 244.60     249.30</p>
<p> Spruce     197.00     190.60   197.60	 192.40     201.00</p>
<p> Birch	239.00     239.40   244.10	 240.70     246.70</p>
<p>An official price agreement has been reached in only one of four raw wood procurement regions. The price levels agreed in southern Finland currently serve as tentative benchmarks in the other regions. Raw wood trade has been very thin recently.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
